{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1350213-help-me-characterize-solar-charm-trees","id":1350213,"title":"Help me characterize Solar Charm trees","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-22T06:05:11-08:00","id":1350213,"title":"Help me characterize Solar Charm trees","content":"Hey, I'm familiar with some solar Charm trees, for example: Melee has three main banches, one for better and more attacks (from Excellent Strike to Iron Whirlwind), one for defense and counterattacks, and one for extra tricks like calling your blade; there's also a minor branch about shooting lazers and damaging Creatures of Darkness.<br /> <br /> But what about Brawl, Archery and Thrown? Can you help me summarize these (or any other solar charm trees). I haven't got much time for studying and selecting charms.<br /> <br /> I appreciate your help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T08:13:27-08:00","id":1350236,"title":"","content":"Generally:<br /> <br /> Brawl is all offense and damn-near no defense. It plays with grappling and onslaught penalties such that getting right up in the enemy's face and keeping their life interesting is highly rewarding.<br /> <br /> Archery is about one-third &quot;shoot regardless of penalties&quot;, one-third &quot;shoot more&quot; and one third &quot;enhance arrows with magic&quot;, with a minor in &quot;create bow and arrows from nothing&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thrown is for sneaky tricksters, mostly. it's the Night Caste's favored method of attack. It has lots of charms for doing gambits better at range )disarm,distract) attacking from stealth, killing silently and so on. The only effects that aren't tricky or sneaky are in a straight line from Triple-Distance Attack Technique to Fiery Solar Chakram.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T08:44:43-08:00","id":1350241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amayad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1350213-help-me-characterize-solar-charm-trees?p=1350236#post1350236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brawl is all offense and damn-near no defense. It plays with grappling and onslaught penalties such that getting right up in the enemy's face and keeping their life interesting is highly rewarding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that Brawl isn't quite &quot;no defense&quot;. Rather, Brawl eschews the usual Defense stats in favor of clashes. A Solar Brawler defends themselves by being better at hitting than the enemy is, pitting skill directly against skill. Brawl has more Clash keyworded charms than any other combat tree, and gets them at earlier Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T09:20:37-08:00","id":1350245,"title":"","content":"Some other charm tree summaries:<br /> <br /> <b>Athletics </b>has four broad sections, one enhancing balance and eventually allowing you to walk across anything and stick to walls; one that boosts running and general foot movement speed; one that boosts jumping and eventually gets into full-on flight; and one (the largest) that increases feats of strength.<br /> <br /> <b>Awareness</b> has three main chains, one boosting each of hearing, sight, and smell/taste, with a short side-branch that boosts Join Battle.<br /> <br /> <b>Bureaucracy </b>has two long chains, one devoted to improving your ability to buy and sell, and the other one to improving or hindering bureaucracies you deal with or lead. There's also a sort of central tree that requires prereqs from both the other two trees, that makes you just a better arguer and debater because you're so good at the rules.<br /> <br /> <b>Craft</b> is actually subdivided into trees &quot;officially&quot; in the core book: Efficiency, Momentum, Repair and Reforging, and Power. Efficiency gives you extra project slots, extra Craft XP, and makes some projects cost less or a lower level of Craft XP. Momentum gives extra craft points for completing projects, and also covers the various tool-replacement and speed-improvement charms. Repair and Reforging is pretty much as described. Power has most of the dice tricks to give more successes on your Craft rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Dodge </b>has a tree that starts mostly by negating penalties to Evasion, but moves into negating successful attacks, getting initiative if you <i>do </i>get hit, and eventually healing some damage you've already taken. It also has a second longer tree, and two short trees, all of which branch off the same prereq charm, Reed in the Wind. The long tree is all about getting initiative from successfully dodging, including stealing it from the enemy, and also has the perfect dodge Seven Shadows Evasion. One of the short trees boosts disengage attempts, while the other boosts reactions to ambushes and surprise attacks, lets you move away from an attacker, and redirect attacks you dodge into someone else.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T16:43:29-08:00","id":1350541,"title":"","content":"Thank you both, this helps me a lot!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T17:05:57-08:00","id":1350546,"title":"","content":"Survival is a giant pet tree, starting with being able to get near any animal and then boosting your pets once you hit e2. With some one offs about food gathering and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T17:51:31-08:00","id":1350555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1350213-help-me-characterize-solar-charm-trees?p=1350546#post1350546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Survival is a giant pet tree, starting with being able to get near any animal and then boosting your pets once you hit e2. With some one offs about food gathering and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>1/4 of Survival is Rambo.<br /> 3/4 of Survival is Pokemon.<br /> <br /> <b>Resistance:</b> The main body of charms is &quot;Juggernaut&quot;.<br /> The three side branches are &quot;Armor Master&quot;, &quot;Immune to sickness&quot;, and &quot;screwing with Initiative and stuff&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: For future reference <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/exalted/comments/3pwiez/exalted_3e_charm_cascades/\" target=\"_blank\">Charm Cascades</a> will help you visualize things more easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 11-23-2019, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T21:06:44-08:00","id":1350763,"title":"","content":"Brawl has 4 trees, which are Block, Hit, Grab, and Power Up. <br /> <br /> Fists of Iron opens up Block<br /> Ferocious Jab starts Hit<br /> Vicious Lunge starts Grab<br /> Thunderclap Rush starts Power Up","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T21:43:54-08:00","id":1350765,"title":"","content":"War has:<br /> <br /> Tiger Warriors: Train others to be badasses!<br /> Divine Army: rally and restore your troops!<br /> Master Planner: Be the General of the Sun!<br /> Warlord genius: Lead your troops to victory!<br /> <br /> Stealth has:<br /> <br /> Super ninja: hide yourself and your anima.<br /> Combat stealth: Kill from the shadows.<br /> One with Darkness: Become a shadow, and move between shadows. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}